WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.590
In 2022, the founder of
the outdoor clothing firm

2
00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:08.400
Patagonia handed its ownership
to a trust and a non-profit body.

3
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.140
Profit not reinvested in the firm
now goes to fighting climate change.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.490
Elsewhere, a new delivery firm
sets its prices below its costs,

5
00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.250
and expects losses for several years.

6
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.410
Neither looks like a firm
trying to make as much

7
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.060
profit as it can.

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.400
So why might a business
choose to earn less

9
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.270
profit than it could?

10
00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:32.280
In this mission, you'll meet the
goals firms chase besides profit,

11
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.470
from growth to survival.

12
00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:37.030
Then you'll weigh up
the case for and against

13
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:39.600
firms taking on social goals.

14
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain why a firm
might set its sights below top profit.
